{"id":"DossierChunk: ure-microtelemetry-service#L36-L36","ruleNumber":null,"rule_number":null,"title":"ure-microtelemetry-service — Pattern 1: Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","headingTitle":"Pattern 1: Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","rawHeading":"Pattern 1: Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","category":"HARVESTED_DOSSIER_CHUNK","sourceTier":"FORENSIC_DOSSIER","epistemicState":"EXTRACTED","confidence":0.75,"confidenceCalibrated":false,"confidenceType":"HEURISTIC_CATEGORY_WEIGHT","domainLetter":null,"domainId":null,"domainName":null,"secondaryDomains":[],"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[36,36],"summary":"### Pattern 1: Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","ruleText":"","whyText":"","whenText":"","fullContent":"### Pattern 1: Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","sourceOccurrences":[{"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[36,36]}],"occurrenceCount":1,"corroborationSources":["ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md"],"isBoilerplate":false,"isIndependentCorroboration":false,"independentCorroborationCount":0,"sourceIndependence":"SINGLE_SOURCE","indexingStatus":"COMPLETE","docLength":13},
{"id":"DossierChunk: ure-microtelemetry-service#L37-L61","ruleNumber":null,"rule_number":null,"title":"ure-microtelemetry-service — Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","headingTitle":"Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","rawHeading":"Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination","category":"HARVESTED_DOSSIER_CHUNK","sourceTier":"FORENSIC_DOSSIER","epistemicState":"EXTRACTED","confidence":0.75,"confidenceCalibrated":false,"confidenceType":"HEURISTIC_CATEGORY_WEIGHT","domainLetter":null,"domainId":null,"domainName":null,"secondaryDomains":[],"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[37,61],"summary":"### Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination **RULE**: Node.js server applications must drain active connections and register explicit SIGTERM and SIGINT listeners to close server sockets and flush pending telemetry before process termination. **WHY**: Prevents dropped in-flight client requests","ruleText":"","whyText":"","whenText":"","fullContent":"### Graceful Process Shutdown Signal Coordination\n**RULE**: Node.js server applications must drain active connections and register explicit SIGTERM and SIGINT listeners to close server sockets and flush pending telemetry before process termination.\n**WHY**: Prevents dropped in-flight client requests, socket hangs, and data loss during container redeployments and rolling updates.\n**WHEN TO APPLY**: All Node.js backend microservices and long-running daemons running in containerized environments (Kubernetes, Docker, Cloud Run).\n**VERIFIED IMPLEMENTATION PATTERN**:\n```javascript\n// Verified implementation pattern from src/index.mjs\nconst shutdown = async (signal) => {\n  console.log(`Received ${signal}, closing active server sockets...`);\n  await app.close();\n  process.exit(0);\n};\nprocess.on('SIGTERM', () => shutdown('SIGTERM'));\nprocess.on('SIGINT', () => shutdown('SIGINT'));\n```\n**NEGATIVE CONSTRAINT**:\n```javascript\n// Anti-pattern to strictly avoid\n// process.exit(0) immediately upon receiving signal, abandoning active HTTP sockets without draining.\n```\n**VERIFICATION METHOD**:\nStatic code analysis and test audit in microtelemetry-service.\n**HIQV DECISION**: CONDITIONAL_PASS (Confidence: 0.87)\n**AUTH TOKEN**: `cf9832eb826e79da...`","sourceOccurrences":[{"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[37,61]}],"occurrenceCount":1,"corroborationSources":["ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md"],"isBoilerplate":false,"isIndependentCorroboration":false,"independentCorroborationCount":0,"sourceIndependence":"SINGLE_SOURCE","indexingStatus":"COMPLETE","docLength":130},
{"id":"DossierChunk: ure-microtelemetry-service#L62-L62","ruleNumber":null,"rule_number":null,"title":"ure-microtelemetry-service — Pattern 2: Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","headingTitle":"Pattern 2: Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","rawHeading":"Pattern 2: Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","category":"HARVESTED_DOSSIER_CHUNK","sourceTier":"FORENSIC_DOSSIER","epistemicState":"EXTRACTED","confidence":0.75,"confidenceCalibrated":false,"confidenceType":"HEURISTIC_CATEGORY_WEIGHT","domainLetter":null,"domainId":null,"domainName":null,"secondaryDomains":[],"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[62,62],"summary":"### Pattern 2: Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","ruleText":"","whyText":"","whenText":"","fullContent":"### Pattern 2: Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","sourceOccurrences":[{"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[62,62]}],"occurrenceCount":1,"corroborationSources":["ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md"],"isBoilerplate":false,"isIndependentCorroboration":false,"independentCorroborationCount":0,"sourceIndependence":"SINGLE_SOURCE","indexingStatus":"COMPLETE","docLength":13},
{"id":"DossierChunk: ure-microtelemetry-service#L63-L87","ruleNumber":null,"rule_number":null,"title":"ure-microtelemetry-service — Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","headingTitle":"Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","rawHeading":"Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant","category":"HARVESTED_DOSSIER_CHUNK","sourceTier":"FORENSIC_DOSSIER","epistemicState":"EXTRACTED","confidence":0.75,"confidenceCalibrated":false,"confidenceType":"HEURISTIC_CATEGORY_WEIGHT","domainLetter":null,"domainId":null,"domainName":null,"secondaryDomains":[],"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[63,87],"summary":"### Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant **RULE**: Application HTTP health endpoints must verify critical internal component readiness (e.g. queue thresholds, buffer capacity) and return HTTP 503 rather than false 200 OK when saturated. **WHY**: Informs orchestrators and load balancers to halt t","ruleText":"","whyText":"","whenText":"","fullContent":"### Multi-Phase Health Check Probe Invariant\n**RULE**: Application HTTP health endpoints must verify critical internal component readiness (e.g. queue thresholds, buffer capacity) and return HTTP 503 rather than false 200 OK when saturated.\n**WHY**: Informs orchestrators and load balancers to halt traffic routing before cascade server failure occurs.\n**WHEN TO APPLY**: All service ingress and health monitoring endpoints across microservice architectures.\n**VERIFIED IMPLEMENTATION PATTERN**:\n```javascript\n// Verified implementation pattern from src/routes/health.mjs\nfastify.get('/health', async (request, reply) => {\n  const isReady = collector.isHealthy();\n  if (!isReady) {\n    return reply.status(503).send({ status: 'UNHEALTHY', reason: 'Collector buffer saturated' });\n  }\n  return reply.status(200).send({ status: 'HEALTHY' });\n});\n```\n**NEGATIVE CONSTRAINT**:\n```javascript\n// Anti-pattern to strictly avoid\n// Returning static HTTP 200 OK unconditionally without verifying underlying subsystem readiness.\n```\n**VERIFICATION METHOD**:\nStatic code analysis and test audit in microtelemetry-service.\n**HIQV DECISION**: CONDITIONAL_PASS (Confidence: 0.87)\n**AUTH TOKEN**: `b3af1160be9ec329...`","sourceOccurrences":[{"filePath":"07_PROJECT_LEARNING/ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md","lineRange":[63,87]}],"occurrenceCount":1,"corroborationSources":["ure-microtelemetry-service-learnings.md"],"isBoilerplate":false,"isIndependentCorroboration":false,"independentCorroborationCount":0,"sourceIndependence":"SINGLE_SOURCE","indexingStatus":"COMPLETE","docLength":128},
